From: ccbench-remote
Subject: [PATCH] taova: let test.py, not genericCC, decide when the flow stops

src/wrappers/taova.py launches genericCC's sender with

    offduration=1 onduration=1000000 traffic_params=deterministic,num_cycles=1

onduration is in MILLISECONDS, so 1000000 = 1000 seconds, and with
num_cycles=1 genericCC sends exactly one on-cycle of that length and then
exits. The wrapper is never told the experiment runtime -- test.py kills the
process group when the clock runs out -- so for any run longer than ~16.7
minutes the sender quits early and test.py keeps the tunnel open over a dead
flow for the remainder.

OBSERVED, 2026-11-04 uplink matrix (-t 3600 --run-times 1):

    taova_datalink_run1.log spans 1000.3 s of a requested 3600 s
    src/analysis/plot.py:119  duration < 0.8 * runtime  -> run discarded
    "Warning: ... had duration 1000.22 seconds but should have been around
     3600 seconds. Ignoring this run."
    pantheon_perf.json == {"taova": {}}

The hour was not salvageable: there is simply no data after minute 16.7.

Fix: raise the on-cycle to 36000000 ms (10 h), longer than any run we will
ask for, so test.py remains the only thing that ends the flow. This does NOT
change the congestion-control algorithm, the RemyCC .dna file, or MIN_RTT; it
only stops genericCC from self-terminating mid-experiment.

--- a/src/wrappers/taova.py
+++ b/src/wrappers/taova.py
@@
-            'offduration=1 onduration=1000000 traffic_params=deterministic,'
+            'offduration=1 onduration=36000000 traffic_params=deterministic,'
